# ============================================================================
# GENERATED DATA DIRECTORIES (regenerated by steps 00a/00/02/03 — not tracked)
# ============================================================================
# Everything under these is reproducible from the pipeline. The CARD homolog
# NOTHING under data/ is tracked — and that is load-bearing, not tidiness.
# On the HPC, $AMR_HOME/{data,results,runs,models,logs} are SYMLINKS to
# /arf/scratch. Git refuses to write tracked paths through a symlink, so any
# tracked file under one of these prefixes makes `git reset --hard` DELETE the
# symlink and replace it with a real directory — silently detaching the repo from
# every genome, matrix and result on scratch. This actually happened on
# 2026-07-15: data/external/blast_db/card_nt/* (8 files) and runs/.gitkeep were
# committed, and the deploy reset severed both links.
#
# The card_nt BLAST DB used to be "the ONE intentional exception", committed so
# step 08 worked out-of-the-box. Step 08 now hard-fails with build instructions
# when the DB is absent (AMR_ALLOW_MISSING_CARD_DB to override), which covers the
# same need without booby-trapping the symlinks. Rebuild it with:
#   makeblastdb -in <card.fna> -dbtype nucl -out data/external/blast_db/card_nt/card
# Do not re-add generated artefacts here; its source FASTA is ignored too.
data/raw/
data/interim/
data/processed/
data/external/blast_db/
# Full CARD data bundle for step 11 (card.json + variant FASTA + built DB; ~40MB)
data/external/card/
# Per-organism metadata produced by 00a/00 (binary phenotype matrix, manifests)
data/external/**/metadata/

# Auto-generated experiment configs (written by step 04 — regenerate, don't track)
config/experiments/**/config_*.yaml

# ============================================================================
# KMC DATABASE FILES
# ============================================================================
*.kmc_pre
*.kmc_suf
*.kmc_tmp

# ============================================================================
# FEATURE MATRICES & LABELS
# ============================================================================
*.npz
# Large k-mer feature matrix files (exceed GitHub's 100MB limit).
# Matches both the legacy layout (data/processed/{ab}/matrix/) and the new
# organism layout (data/processed/{organism}/{ab}/matrix/).
**/matrix/features.txt

# Legacy / antibiotic-specific data directories (pre-Cookiecutter layout).
# These hold generated per-antibiotic artefacts and must never be committed.
data/ampicillin/
data/cefotaxime/
data/ciprofloxacin/
data/gentamicin/

